{"name": "filtered_scheduler_binding", "kind": "filtered", "why": "The scheduler binds a ReplicaSet-shaped pod: same resource and an explicit objectRef.name of the controller shape, but objectRef.subresource=binding. Removing the subresource filter fires branch (a); the binding subresource alone suppresses it. The benign corpus carries ~30 such scheduler bindings with ReplicaSet-shaped names.", "source": "real: local kube-apiserver v1.36.4 lab, POST pods/<name>/binding for trr9031-api-6f6b679f8f-x7k2q (verb=create, subresource=binding).", "events": [{"kind": "Event", "apiVersion": "audit.k8s.io/v1", "level": "Metadata", "auditID": "e24f748a-c576-43ee-b945-81f24f806777", "stage": "ResponseComplete", "requestURI": "/api/v1/namespaces/trr9031/pods/trr9031-api-6f6b679f8f-x7k2q/binding", "verb": "create", "user": {"username": "kubernetes-admin", "uid": "uid-admin", "groups": ["kubeadm:cluster-admins", "system:masters", "system:authenticated"]}, "sourceIPs": ["127.0.0.1"], "userAgent": "kubectl/v1.36.4 (linux/amd64) kubernetes/bb826b1", "objectRef": {"resource": "pods", "namespace": "trr9031", "name": "trr9031-api-6f6b679f8f-x7k2q", "apiVersion": "v1", "subresource": "binding"}, "responseStatus": {"metadata": {}, "status": "Success", "code": 201}, "requestReceivedTimestamp": "2026-11-01T02:55:29.129742Z", "stageTimestamp": "2026-11-01T02:55:29.134042Z", "annotations": {"authorization.k8s.io/decision": "allow", "authorization.k8s.io/reason": ""}}], "breaks": ["filter_subresource.objectRef.subresource"]}
{"name": "filtered_pod_exec_system_ns", "kind": "filtered", "why": "An exec into the kube-system pod trr9031-proxy-x7k2q: same resource, a DaemonSet-shaped name in a system namespace, but objectRef.subresource=exec. Removing the subresource filter fires branch (c); the exec subresource alone suppresses it. This is the pods/exec-on-a-system-namespace-pod case the SigmaHQ 'Creation Of Pod In System Namespace' rule fires on and this rule does not.", "source": "real: local kube-apiserver v1.36.4 lab, `kubectl exec` on trr9031-proxy-x7k2q in kube-system (verb=create, subresource=exec).", "events": [{"kind": "Event", "apiVersion": "audit.k8s.io/v1", "level": "Metadata", "auditID": "5eafeb6d-1485-440a-b162-e3bcb50ec532", "stage": "ResponseStarted", "requestURI": "/api/v1/namespaces/kube-system/pods/trr9031-proxy-x7k2q/exec?command=ls&container=c&stderr=true&stdout=true", "verb": "create", "user": {"username": "kubernetes-admin", "uid": "uid-admin", "groups": ["kubeadm:cluster-admins", "system:masters", "system:authenticated"]}, "sourceIPs": ["127.0.0.1"], "userAgent": "kubectl/v1.36.4 (linux/amd64) kubernetes/bb826b1", "objectRef": {"resource": "pods", "namespace": "kube-system", "name": "trr9031-proxy-x7k2q", "apiVersion": "v1", "subresource": "exec"}, "responseStatus": {"metadata": {}, "status": "Failure", "message": "pod trr9031-proxy-x7k2q does not have a host assigned", "reason": "BadRequest", "code": 400}, "requestReceivedTimestamp": "2026-11-01T02:55:29.063860Z", "stageTimestamp": "2026-11-01T02:55:29.065342Z", "annotations": {"authorization.k8s.io/decision": "allow", "authorization.k8s.io/reason": ""}}], "breaks": ["filter_subresource.objectRef.subresource"]}
{"name": "filtered_kubelet_mirror_pod", "kind": "filtered", "why": "A kubelet mirror pod of a static pod, created by system:node, with a DaemonSet-shaped name in kube-system (the pathological case where the node name is five vowel-free characters, so the mirror name <staticpod>-<node> matches the '-<5>' shape). The rule excludes system:node, so removing the filter_node filter fires branch (c); the node identity alone suppresses it. Real mirror pods have node-suffixed names that normally carry vowels and do not match the shape (see confounder_kubelet_mirror_pod).", "source": "synthetic (built from the real kube-system create shape): a kubelet mirror pod cache-wk2x7 by system:node:wk2x7, with the kubernetes.io/config.mirror annotation. Shape cites pkg/kubelet/pod mirror-pod creation (v1.36.4).", "events": [{"kind": "Event", "apiVersion": "audit.k8s.io/v1", "level": "Request", "auditID": "3a7c1e94-0b2d-4f61-9c83-1d2e3f405162", "stage": "ResponseComplete", "requestURI": "/api/v1/namespaces/kube-system/pods", "verb": "create", "user": {"username": "system:node:wk2x7", "groups": ["system:nodes", "system:authenticated"], "uid": "uid-wk2x7"}, "sourceIPs": ["192.0.2.50"], "userAgent": "kubelet/v1.36.4 (linux/amd64) kubernetes/bb826b1", "objectRef": {"resource": "pods", "namespace": "kube-system", "name": "cache-wk2x7", "apiVersion": "v1"}, "responseStatus": {"metadata": {}, "code": 201}, "requestObject": {"kind": "Pod", "apiVersion": "v1", "metadata": {"name": "cache-wk2x7", "namespace": "kube-system", "annotations": {"kubernetes.io/config.mirror": "a1b2c3d4e5", "kubernetes.io/config.source": "file"}}, "spec": {"nodeName": "wk2x7", "containers": [{"name": "c", "image": "registry.k8s.io/pause:3.10"}]}, "status": {}}, "requestReceivedTimestamp": "2026-11-01T03:08:22.837897Z", "stageTimestamp": "2026-11-01T03:08:22.845568Z", "annotations": {"authorization.k8s.io/decision": "allow", "authorization.k8s.io/reason": "", "pod-security.kubernetes.io/enforce-policy": "privileged:latest"}}], "breaks": ["filter_node.user.username"]}
{"name": "filtered_node_debugger", "kind": "filtered", "why": "A node-debugger pod created by `kubectl debug node` targeting a control-plane node with an explicit -n kube-system: objectRef.name node-debugger-<node>-<5> matches the '-<5>' shape in a system namespace, by a human. The filter_node_debugger filter excludes the node-debugger- prefix; removing it fires branch (c). Naming a backdoor node-debugger-* abandons the system-workload masquerade, so the filter is not an evasion of the technique.", "source": "real: local kube-apiserver v1.36.4 lab, a pause pod node-debugger-kind-control-plane-x7k2q in kube-system (the name kubectl debug node writes, debug.go:721 at v1.36.4).", "events": [{"kind": "Event", "apiVersion": "audit.k8s.io/v1", "level": "Request", "auditID": "f66c32cf-9e3c-4709-a522-beda4645c6da", "stage": "ResponseComplete", "requestURI": "/api/v1/namespaces/kube-system/pods?fieldManager=kubectl-run", "verb": "create", "user": {"username": "kubernetes-admin", "uid": "uid-admin", "groups": ["kubeadm:cluster-admins", "system:masters", "system:authenticated"]}, "sourceIPs": ["127.0.0.1"], "userAgent": "kubectl/v1.36.4 (linux/amd64) kubernetes/bb826b1", "objectRef": {"resource": "pods", "namespace": "kube-system", "name": "node-debugger-kind-control-plane-x7k2q", "apiVersion": "v1"}, "responseStatus": {"metadata": {}, "code": 201}, "requestObject": {"kind": "Pod", "apiVersion": "v1", "metadata": {"name": "node-debugger-kind-control-plane-x7k2q", "labels": {"run": "node-debugger-kind-control-plane-x7k2q"}}, "spec": {"containers": [{"name": "node-debugger-kind-control-plane-x7k2q", "image": "registry.k8s.io/pause:3.10", "resources": {}, "terminationMessagePath": "/dev/termination-log", "terminationMessagePolicy": "File", "imagePullPolicy": "IfNotPresent"}], "restartPolicy": "Never", "terminationGracePeriodSeconds": 30, "dnsPolicy": "ClusterFirst", "securityContext": {}, "schedulerName": "default-scheduler", "enableServiceLinks": true}, "status": {}}, "requestReceivedTimestamp": "2026-11-01T03:01:48.983412Z", "stageTimestamp": "2026-11-01T03:01:48.999705Z", "annotations": {"authorization.k8s.io/decision": "allow", "authorization.k8s.io/reason": "", "pod-security.kubernetes.io/enforce-policy": "privileged:latest"}}], "breaks": ["filter_node_debugger.objectRef.name"]}
{"name": "confounder_controller_create", "kind": "confounder", "why": "A REAL ReplicaSet-controller pod create: same verb, resource and no subresource, and requestObject.metadata.generateName (lookalike-demo-65bb645ff8-) in exactly the controller shape, but NO objectRef.name (the API server copies objectRef.name from metadata.name before it appends the random suffix, and a controller create has no metadata.name). Both name branches read objectRef.name, so neither fires. This is why the rule keys on an explicit objectRef.name, not on generateName; keying on generateName would fire on every controller create (RULE_DEFECTS.md KTBD-K1).", "source": "real: local kube-apiserver v1.36.4 lab, the kube-controller-manager's own pod create for Deployment lookalike-demo (verb=create, no subresource, no objectRef.name).", "events": [{"kind": "Event", "apiVersion": "audit.k8s.io/v1", "level": "Request", "auditID": "9d1fe301-e8eb-4ee5-8342-ecf1542b1bf4", "stage": "ResponseComplete", "requestURI": "/api/v1/namespaces/trr9031/pods", "verb": "create", "user": {"username": "system:kube-controller-manager", "uid": "uid-kcm", "groups": ["system:masters", "system:authenticated"]}, "sourceIPs": ["127.0.0.1"], "userAgent": "kube-controller-manager/v1.36.4 (linux/amd64) kubernetes/bb826b1/replicaset-controller", "objectRef": {"resource": "pods", "namespace": "trr9031", "apiVersion": "v1"}, "responseStatus": {"metadata": {}, "code": 201}, "requestObject": {"kind": "Pod", "apiVersion": "v1", "metadata": {"generateName": "lookalike-demo-65bb645ff8-", "labels": {"app": "lookalike-demo", "pod-template-hash": "65bb645ff8"}, "ownerReferences": [{"apiVersion": "apps/v1", "kind": "ReplicaSet", "name": "lookalike-demo-65bb645ff8", "uid": "cf3635e9-a292-4991-b2e7-d6fb62fabdbe", "controller": true, "blockOwnerDeletion": true}]}, "spec": {"containers": [{"name": "c", "image": "registry.k8s.io/pause:3.10", "resources": {}, "terminationMessagePath": "/dev/termination-log", "terminationMessagePolicy": "File", "imagePullPolicy": "IfNotPresent"}], "restartPolicy": "Always", "terminationGracePeriodSeconds": 30, "dnsPolicy": "ClusterFirst", "securityContext": {}, "schedulerName": "default-scheduler", "enableServiceLinks": true}, "status": {}}, "requestReceivedTimestamp": "2026-11-01T02:53:55.790646Z", "stageTimestamp": "2026-11-01T02:53:55.795614Z", "annotations": {"authorization.k8s.io/decision": "allow", "authorization.k8s.io/reason": "", "pod-security.kubernetes.io/enforce-policy": "privileged:latest"}}]}
